  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for people who can be trusted with work. They judge you by reliability, communication and how you handle mistakes.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is delivering a small task on time and telling the other person it is done.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and employability skills for graduates: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft messages and summarise notes. Routine drafting shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Trust, communication and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and check; later, own the outcome.
  </p>

